{
  "schemaVersion": 3,
  "lessonTitle": "The Definite Integral",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q-int-def-ex3",
      "stem": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "latex": "Write the definite integral $\\displaystyle\\int_1^4 \\sqrt{x}\\,dx$ as a limit of a right-endpoint Riemann sum."
        }
      ],
      "parts": [
        {
          "id": "q-int-def-ex3-a",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "latex": "Which expression is the limit definition of the definite integral $\\displaystyle\\int_a^b f(x)\\,dx$?"
            }
          ],
          "summary": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\int_a^b f(x) \\,dx = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\sum_{k=1}^n f(x_k^*)\\,\\Delta x$"
            }
          ],
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-a-c1",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\sum_{k=1}^n f(x_k^*)\\,\\Delta x$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": false,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "This is a Riemann sum, but the definite integral takes the limit as $n \\to \\infty$."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-a-c2",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\sum_{k=1}^n f(x_k^*)$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": false,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "Each height must be multiplied by the width $\\Delta x$ of a subinterval."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-a-c3",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\sum_{k=1}^n f(x_k^*)\\,\\Delta x$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": true,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "The definite integral is the limit of a Riemann sum. In the summation, each height $f(x_k^*)$ is multiplied by the width $\\Delta x$."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-int-def-ex3-b",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "latex": "Splitting $[1,4]$ into $n$ equal subintervals, what is the width $\\Delta x$ of each subinterval?"
            }
          ],
          "summary": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "latex": "$\\Delta x = \\dfrac{3}{n}$"
            }
          ],
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-b-c1",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\Delta x = \\dfrac{3}{n}$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": true,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$\\Delta x = \\dfrac{b-a}{n} = \\dfrac{4-1}{n} = \\dfrac{3}{n}$."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-b-c2",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\Delta x = \\dfrac{4}{n}$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": false,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "Use $\\Delta x = \\dfrac{b-a}{n}$ with $a = 1$ and $b = 4$, not just $b$."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-b-c3",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\Delta x = \\dfrac{n}{3}$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": false,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "The width is $\\dfrac{b-a}{n}$, so $n$ belongs in the denominator."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-int-def-ex3-c",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "latex": "Which formula gives the right endpoint $x_k^*$ for a right-endpoint Riemann sum?"
            }
          ],
          "summary": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "latex": "$x_k^* = a + k\\,\\Delta x$"
            }
          ],
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-c-c1",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$x_k^* = a + (k-1)\\,\\Delta x$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": false,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "That formula gives the left endpoints of each subinterval."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-c-c2",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$x_k^* = a + \\left(k - \\tfrac{1}{2}\\right)\\Delta x$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": false,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "That formula gives the midpoints of each subinterval."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-c-c3",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$x_k^* = a + k\\,\\Delta x$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": true,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "Right endpoints take $k$ steps of size $\\Delta x$ starting from $a$."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-int-def-ex3-d",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "latex": "Substituting $a = 1$ and $\\Delta x = \\dfrac{3}{n}$, what are the right endpoints $x_k^* = a + k\\,\\Delta x$?"
            }
          ],
          "summary": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "latex": "$x_k^* = 1 + \\dfrac{3k}{n}$"
            }
          ],
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-d-c1",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$x_k^* = \\dfrac{3k}{n}$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": false,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "Don't forget to add the left endpoint $a = 1$."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-d-c2",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$x_k^* = 1 + \\dfrac{3(k-1)}{n}$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": false,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "That uses the left-endpoint formula $a + (k-1)\\,\\Delta x$."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-d-c3",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$x_k^* = 1 + \\dfrac{3k}{n}$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": true,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$x_k^* = 1 + k \\cdot \\dfrac{3}{n} = 1 + \\dfrac{3k}{n}$."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-int-def-ex3-e",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "latex": "Putting this all together, what is $\\displaystyle\\int_1^4 \\sqrt{x}\\,dx$ written as a limit of a Riemann sum?"
            }
          ],
          "summary": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\int_1^4 \\sqrt{x} \\,dx = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\sum_{k=1}^n \\sqrt{1 + \\dfrac{3k}{n}}\\cdot \\dfrac{3}{n}$"
            }
          ],
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-e-c1",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\sum_{k=1}^n \\sqrt{1 + \\dfrac{3k}{n}}\\cdot \\dfrac{3}{n}$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": false,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "This is the Riemann sum. Now take the limit as $n \\to \\infty$ to get the definite integral."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-e-c2",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\sum_{k=1}^n \\sqrt{1 + \\dfrac{3k}{n}}\\cdot \\dfrac{3}{n}$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": true,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "Substitute $x_k^* = 1 + \\dfrac{3k}{n}$ into $f(x) = \\sqrt{x}$ for the height, and multiply by $\\Delta x = \\dfrac{3}{n}$."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q-int-def-ex3-e-c3",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\sum_{k=1}^n \\Bigl(1 + \\dfrac{3k}{n}\\Bigr) \\cdot \\dfrac{3}{n}$"
                }
              ],
              "correct": false,
              "feedback": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "latex": "The height is $f(x_k^*) = \\sqrt{x_k^*} = \\sqrt{1 + \\frac{3k}{n}}$, rather than $1 + \\frac{3k}{n}$."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "conclusion": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "latex": "Putting it all together, $\\displaystyle\\int_1^4 \\sqrt{x}\\,dx = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\sum_{k=1}^n \\sqrt{1 + \\dfrac{3k}{n}}\\cdot \\dfrac{3}{n}.$"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}